      },
      "message": "fix(motion): one flat plane per closed opening's lid\n\nThe closing levels a lid's cells a hair apart on any model whose\nsurface is not flat, and emitting each cell its own level tiled the\nlid as steps. Across a step edge the ball can seat on neither plane\nfor a full ball-width annulus - the higher lid top blocks it from the\nlower, and a lid top's free edge carries no fold support - so support\ngoes None and every step costs a retract and plunge: 166 feeds near\nthe bolt holes on the report's model, against 22 with the fill off.\n\nLift the whole lid - raised component and one-cell ring - to the\nhighest closed height over its cells before emitting, one plane per\nopening. The plateau runs after the enclosed check, so enclosure is\nstill judged on the closing's own levels. Measured on the report's\nmodel: 40 feeds near the holes, 57 elsewhere.",
